{
    "map": {
        "angle_threshold.descr": "<xdoc><p>The angle formed by the incident segments over which the vertex related to these segments will be reduced. The wider the angle, the fewer number of vertices will be reduced. The default is 160 degrees. This parameter is active when <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Reshape Operation</span> is <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Reduce vertices by angle</span>.</p></xdoc>",
        "angle_threshold.title": "Angle Threshold",
        "are_containers_preserved.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies how the algorithm will process containers.<ul><li>Checked—The layout algorithm will apply to the top graph of the diagram so containers are preserved.</li><li>Unchecked—The layout algorithm will apply to both content and noncontent features in the diagram. This is the default.</li></ul></p></xdoc>",
        "are_containers_preserved.title": "Preserve container layout",
        "breakpoint_absolute.descr": "<xdoc><p>The maximum distance between each junction to the first or last break point along edges incident to that junction when those edges are squared. The default is 8.66 in the units of the diagram&apos;s coordinate system. This parameter is active when <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Reshape Operation</span> is <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Square edges</span>.</p></xdoc>",
        "breakpoint_absolute.title": "Break Point Position",
        "circular_arc_position.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the segment on which a circular arc will be placed.</p><ul><li><span title=\"LEFT_OF_VERTICAL_SEGMENT\">Left of vertical segment</span>—A circular arc will be placed to the left of the vertical segment.</li><li><span title=\"RIGHT_OF_VERTICAL_SEGMENT\">Right of vertical segment</span>—A circular arc will be placed to the right of the vertical segment.</li><li><span title=\"ABOVE_HORIZONTAL_SEGMENT\">Above horizontal segment</span>—A circular arc will be placed above the horizontal segment.</li><li><span title=\"BELOW_HORIZONTAL_SEGMENT\">Below horizontal segment</span>—A circular arc will be placed below the horizontal segment.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "circular_arc_position.domain.ABOVE_HORIZONTAL_SEGMENT": "Above horizontal segment",
        "circular_arc_position.domain.BELOW_HORIZONTAL_SEGMENT": "Below horizontal segment",
        "circular_arc_position.domain.LEFT_OF_VERTICAL_SEGMENT": "Left of vertical segment",
        "circular_arc_position.domain.RIGHT_OF_VERTICAL_SEGMENT": "Right of vertical segment",
        "circular_arc_position.title": "Circular Arc Position",
        "circular_arc_radius.descr": "The radius of the circular arc that will be added to the crossing edge locations. The default is 5.",
        "circular_arc_radius.title": "Circular Arc Radius",
        "description": "Processes simple operations on vertices along edges.",
        "in_network_diagram_layer.descr": "The network diagram to which the layout will be applied.",
        "in_network_diagram_layer.title": "Input Network Diagram Layer",
        "is_path_preserved.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies whether vertices along the edges that will be squared will be preserved. This parameter is active when <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Reshape Operation</span> is <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Square edges</span>.<ul><li>Checked—The direction of any edge will be considered, and vertices along that edge will be preserved from the first vertex to the last. This is the default.</li><li>Unchecked—Vertices along the diagram edges will not be considered, and the vertices will be removed.</li></ul></p></xdoc>",
        "is_path_preserved.title": "Preserve path",
        "offset_between_segment_absolute.descr": "<xdoc><p>The spacing that will separate parallel segments of squared edges incident to the same junction. The default is 5 in the units of the diagram&apos;s coordinate system. This parameter is active when <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Reshape Operation</span> is <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Square edges</span>.</p></xdoc>",
        "offset_between_segment_absolute.title": "Offset Between Edges",
        "out_network_diagram_layer.title": "Output Network Diagram",
        "params.category1": "Advanced Options",
        "reshape_type.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies how edges will be reshaped.</p><ul><li><span title=\"REMOVE_VERTICES\">Remove vertices</span>—Vertices along edges in the diagram will be removed.</li><li><span title=\"SQUARE_EDGES\">Square edges</span>—Vertices will be placed along diagram edges, and the edges will be displayed with right angles. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"SEPARATE_OVERLAPPING_EDGES\">Separate overlapping edges</span>—Edges that connect the same origin and extremity junctions will be separated when they are overlapping.</li><li><span title=\"REDUCE_VERTICES_BY_ANGLE\">Reduce vertices by angle</span>—Some or all vertices displayed along diagram edges will be reduced according to the angle that separates the segments incident to those vertices.</li><li><span title=\"MARK_CROSSING_EDGES\">Mark crossing edges</span>—The horizontal and vertical diagram edges that cross each other at a right angle in the diagram will be marked, and the geometry of one of the crossing edges will be reshaped to display a circular arc at this location.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "reshape_type.domain.MARK_CROSSING_EDGES": "Mark crossing edges",
        "reshape_type.domain.REDUCE_VERTICES_BY_ANGLE": "Reduce vertices by angle",
        "reshape_type.domain.REMOVE_VERTICES": "Remove vertices",
        "reshape_type.domain.SEPARATE_OVERLAPPING_EDGES": "Separate overlapping edges",
        "reshape_type.domain.SQUARE_EDGES": "Square edges",
        "reshape_type.title": "Reshape Operation",
        "run_async.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies whether the layout algorithm will run asynchronously or synchronously on the server.<ul><li>Checked—The layout algorithm will run asynchronously on the server. This option dedicates server resources to run the layout algorithm with a longer time-out. Running asynchronously is recommended for layouts that are time consuming and may exceed the server time-out (for example, Partial Overlapping Edges) and applying to large diagrams (more than 25,000 features).</li><li>Unchecked—The layout algorithm will run synchronously on the server. It can fail without completion if it exceeds the service default time-out value of 600 seconds. This is the default.</li></ul></p></xdoc>",
        "run_async.title": "Run in asynchronous mode on the server",
        "shift_between_edge_absolute.descr": "<xdoc><p>The absolute spacing that will separate two edges. The default is 0.5 in the units of the diagram&apos;s coordinate system. This parameter is active when <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Reshape Operation</span> is <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Separate overlapping edges</span>.</p></xdoc>",
        "shift_between_edge_absolute.title": "Offset Between Edges",
        "summary": "<xdoc><p>Processes simple operations on vertices along edges.</p><note type=\"caution\"/><p group=\"note\">If you have an open edit session, you must save your edits prior to running this tool. This ensures that the diagram reflects the latest changes made to the network topology in the database. If you fail to save your edits, the edits will not be reflected in the diagram.</p><note type=\"note\"/><p group=\"note\">Each layout algorithm includes default parameter values. The default parameter values will be used unless otherwise specified. If the input network diagram is based on a template for which this layout has been configured with a different parameter value, that value will be used instead.</p></xdoc>",
        "title": "Reshape Diagram Edges Layout"
    }
}
